# %% [markdown]
# # DriftSense — 06: Root-Cause Attribution Engine & Benchmark
#
# **Runtime Type:** Python 3 (CPU or GPU)  
# **Estimated Runtime:** ~1-2 minutes  
# **RAM Needed:** ~2-4 GB  
# **Disk Needed:** ~1 GB  
# **Expected Outputs:**  
# - Attributor Checkpoints: `runs/<run_id>/models/{random,prior,correlation,xgboost}.joblib`  
# - Validation Attributions Matrix: `runs/<run_id>/val_attributions.csv`  
# - Validation Attribution Metrics Report: `runs/<run_id>/val_attribute_metrics.json`  
# - Anomaly Labels & Operational Events Tables: `runs/<run_id>/val_anomaly_labels.json`, `runs/<run_id>/val_operational_events.json`  
# - Attribution Visualizations: `runs/<run_id>/attribution_comparison.png`  
# - Cryptographically Verified Manifest: `runs/<run_id>/manifest.json`  
#
# > **CRITICAL EVALUATION & ISOLATION INVARIANTS (G6 & A8.4):**  
# > - **Canonical Cause Taxonomy (Contract 10):** All predictions map to the 6 canonical cause categories (`DEPLOYMENT_DEFECT`, `AUTOSCALING_OVERPROVISION`, `CONFIG_MODIFICATION`, `EXTERNAL_TRAFFIC_SURGE`, `ORPHANED_STORAGE_ACCUMULATION`, `RUNAWAY_BATCH_PROCESS`).  
# > - **Decoy Event Isolation (Generator Design §3A):** Attributors must discriminate between causal events and benign operations ($E_{\text{decoy}}$) that occur concurrently without cost impact.  
# > - **Multi-Cause Cascades (Generator Design §3C):** Multi-label ranking evaluates both primary and contributing causes.  
# > - **A8.4 Test Quarantine:** The test partition ($D_{\text{test}}$, Days 25–30) is strictly locked. No attributions are generated or evaluated on test data.

